WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.160
An AI inference cluster is an operational system, not simply a collection of GPUs.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:12.900
Its design begins with users, models, data sensitivity, latency, throughput, concurrency, uptime, and budget.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.240
Those requirements determine whether a cluster is justified at all.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:22.780
A single server remains the better answer when it can meet demand with acceptable recovery and less management overhead.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.400
When scale-out is justified, choose the simplest architecture that satisfies it.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:36.260
Use stable model servers behind a controlled interface, route requests only to compatible healthy nodes, and make queueing and overload behavior explicit.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:49.120
Match GPUs and VRAM to model roles, support them with sufficient CPU, RAM, storage, network capacity, power, and cooling, and understand where consumer components trade lower cost for fewer operational features.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:55.340
Manage model weights, tokenizers, templates, runtimes, and configuration as versioned releases.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:02.600
Keep active models in local worker caches when that improves startup and resilience, while maintaining an approved source of truth.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:08.100
Separate those artifacts from prompts, embeddings, logs, and private datasets.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.080
Back up irreplaceable configuration and data, and test recovery.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.260
Finally, secure and observe the whole service.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:24.280
Authenticate clients, segment management paths, protect secrets, control patches, and monitor both user experience and hardware health.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.340
Build rollback and incident response into routine operations.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:35.200
Start with measured demand, establish a repeatable baseline, and scale the component that evidence identifies as the bottleneck.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:41.180
That discipline produces a cluster that delivers dependable capacity instead of multiplying cost and failure modes.
